  "reason": "The current best is config_006 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) at 0.653. All RNA-only variants with weaker encoders (pca_n2000, scgpt) are clearly inferior, leaving little room for RNA-only refinement. The critical untested question is whether multimodal fusion can push beyond 0.653. Image-only resnet50 was very weak (0.208), but fusion with a strong RNA backbone may still extract complementary spatial information. I choose config_033 (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, resnet50, transformer, weighted) because: (1) it pairs the best-known RNA setup (scvi_n200 + multiprofile + transformer) with the image modality to directly test the fusion hypothesis; (2) weighted fusion is the safest choice given the uncertain image quality—it can learn to downweight a weak image signal rather than being forced to process it equally as with concat; (3) resnet50 is already characterized (0.208), making the multimodal result interpretable as a clean fusion effect; (4) with 3 experiments remaining, if this beats 0.653 we can immediately try ViT-L next, and if it does not, we confirm RNA-only is optimal and avoid wasting budget on further multimodal variants with a known-weak encoder."
}

